1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,550
StreamField, properly.

2
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:08,804
Right now the body of every page is a single rich text field.

3
00:00:08,804 --> 00:00:09,388
One box.

4
00:00:09,388 --> 00:00:13,258
The editor can put anything they like in it, and you,

5
00:00:13,258 --> 00:00:15,668
the person who designed the site,

6
00:00:15,668 --> 00:00:19,392
have no say at all in what comes out the other end.

7
00:00:20,192 --> 00:00:21,881
So what is StreamField.

8
00:00:21,881 --> 00:00:24,597
It is not a fancier rich text editor.

9
00:00:24,597 --> 00:00:29,002
It is a JSON column holding an ordered list of typed blocks.

10
00:00:29,002 --> 00:00:32,085
Hold on to the JSON part of that sentence,

11
00:00:32,085 --> 00:00:37,298
because it explains an error we are going to hit in about four minutes.

12
00:00:38,098 --> 00:00:42,715
There are four kinds of block and they nest inside each other.

13
00:00:42,715 --> 00:00:44,650
Primitives hold one value.

14
00:00:44,650 --> 00:00:48,895
A struct block is a record: these fields belong together.

15
00:00:48,895 --> 00:00:52,767
A list block is a repeat: several of the same thing.

16
00:00:52,767 --> 00:00:57,532
And a stream block is a choice: pick any of these, in any order.

17
00:00:57,532 --> 00:01:00,436
That last one is the body field itself.

18
00:01:01,236 --> 00:01:04,532
These two are the ones everybody confuses.

19
00:01:04,532 --> 00:01:10,576
A service has a name and a description, and those two always travel together,

20
00:01:10,576 --> 00:01:12,616
so that is a struct block.

21
00:01:12,616 --> 00:01:17,640
A studio offers several services, so we wrap it in a list block.

22
00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:19,052
Struct, then list.

23
00:01:19,052 --> 00:01:20,622
Record, then repeat.

24
00:01:21,422 --> 00:01:23,467
Here is the first real block.

25
00:01:23,467 --> 00:01:26,077
A quote, and an optional attribution.

26
00:01:26,077 --> 00:01:28,686
The fields are constructor arguments.

27
00:01:28,686 --> 00:01:34,328
Everything in Meta is about presentation: the icon that shows in the block menu,

28
00:01:34,328 --> 00:01:40,040
the label the editor reads, and the template it renders through on the front end.

29
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:43,905
And this is the pattern worth remembering.

30
00:01:43,905 --> 00:01:46,750
A struct block containing a list block.

31
00:01:46,750 --> 00:01:52,296
A heading that appears once, and then between one and six services under it.

32
00:01:52,296 --> 00:01:56,674
Min num and max num are the guard rails you hand the client.

33
00:01:57,474 --> 00:02:00,290
And the top level block collects them.

34
00:02:00,290 --> 00:02:03,996
Five things an editor is allowed to add to a page.

35
00:02:03,996 --> 00:02:06,590
Notice rich text has not gone away.

36
00:02:06,590 --> 00:02:12,297
It is still here, it is just one block among several now instead of being the

37
00:02:12,297 --> 00:02:13,260
entire field.

38
00:02:14,060 --> 00:02:17,941
The model change is two lines, on both page types.

39
00:02:17,941 --> 00:02:22,832
And the content panel underneath does not change one character.

40
00:02:22,832 --> 00:02:26,558
It is still just a field panel pointing at body.

41
00:02:27,358 --> 00:02:29,633
One warning before we migrate.

42
00:02:29,633 --> 00:02:35,701
Nearly every StreamField tutorial you will find tells you to pass use json field

43
00:02:35,701 --> 00:02:36,611
equals true.

44
00:02:36,611 --> 00:02:39,266
That was needed before Wagtail six.

45
00:02:39,266 --> 00:02:45,334
In seven point four the parameter is still accepted and, in Wagtail's own words,

46
00:02:45,334 --> 00:02:45,940
ignored.

47
00:02:45,940 --> 00:02:48,064
Don't type it into new code.

48
00:02:48,864 --> 00:02:49,205
So.

49
00:02:49,205 --> 00:02:53,973
Make migrations, migrate, and it blows up.

50
00:02:53,973 --> 00:02:55,789
Integrity error.

51
00:02:55,789 --> 00:02:58,514
Check constraint failed.

52
00:02:58,514 --> 00:03:00,330
JSON valid body.

53
00:03:01,130 --> 00:03:05,308
And nothing in that message says the word StreamField.

54
00:03:05,308 --> 00:03:07,011
Here is what it means.

55
00:03:07,011 --> 00:03:11,808
Back in episode three you typed some text into the About page,

56
00:03:11,808 --> 00:03:14,981
so that column holds a paragraph of HTML.

57
00:03:14,981 --> 00:03:19,623
The new column is JSON, and a paragraph of HTML is not JSON.

58
00:03:19,623 --> 00:03:23,492
Every single person following along will hit this.

59
00:03:24,292 --> 00:03:27,251
And before you panic: nothing is broken.

60
00:03:27,251 --> 00:03:30,580
Django runs a migration inside a transaction,

61
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:34,205
so when it failed it rolled the whole thing back.

62
00:03:34,205 --> 00:03:37,756
Show migrations still lists 0004 as not applied,

63
00:03:37,756 --> 00:03:40,790
and your content is exactly where it was.

64
00:03:40,790 --> 00:03:46,486
On Postgres you get a different message for the same cause, and the same fix.

65
00:03:47,286 --> 00:03:51,795
The fix is to hand edit the migration Django just generated,

66
00:03:51,795 --> 00:03:55,703
and convert the data before the column changes type.

67
00:03:55,703 --> 00:03:57,958
The order is the entire trick.

68
00:03:57,958 --> 00:04:02,316
That run python runs while the column is still plain text,

69
00:04:02,316 --> 00:04:06,600
so it can read the HTML out and write valid JSON back in.

70
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:08,579
And this is it.

71
00:04:08,579 --> 00:04:14,238
Take whatever HTML is in the field, wrap it as a single paragraph block,

72
00:04:14,238 --> 00:04:16,281
and write it back as JSON.

73
00:04:16,281 --> 00:04:20,997
Note the shape of a block: a type, a value, and a unique id.

74
00:04:20,997 --> 00:04:26,263
That id matters, it is how Wagtail tracks a block across revisions.

75
00:04:26,263 --> 00:04:28,699
Write the reverse function too.

76
00:04:28,699 --> 00:04:32,786
It is six more lines and it means you can undo this.

77
00:04:33,586 --> 00:04:35,952
Run it again, and it applies.

78
00:04:35,952 --> 00:04:41,908
And the About page's paragraph is still there, now living inside a block.

79
00:04:42,708 --> 00:04:47,461
While we are in there, the rest of that file looks horrifying.

80
00:04:47,461 --> 00:04:51,217
That is Wagtail seven's compact migration format.

81
00:04:51,217 --> 00:04:56,582
Every block definition is written once and then referred to by number.

82
00:04:56,582 --> 00:04:59,572
It is unreadable and it is meant to be.

83
00:04:59,572 --> 00:05:01,718
Nobody hand edits that half.

84
00:05:01,718 --> 00:05:03,558
We only touched the top.

85
00:05:04,358 --> 00:05:07,162
The page templates get one line shorter.

86
00:05:07,162 --> 00:05:12,701
The rich text filter goes, because StreamField renders every block through that

87
00:05:12,701 --> 00:05:14,173
block's own template.

88
00:05:14,173 --> 00:05:17,048
There is nothing left for a filter to do.

89
00:05:17,848 --> 00:05:20,333
And a block template is tiny.

90
00:05:20,333 --> 00:05:24,188
Inside one, the block is always called value,

91
00:05:24,188 --> 00:05:28,301
and a struct block's fields hang off it by name.

92
00:05:28,301 --> 00:05:30,957
value.quote, value.attribution.

93
00:05:30,957 --> 00:05:32,842
That is the whole API.

94
00:05:33,642 --> 00:05:37,038
And here is this episode's ten minute lesson.

95
00:05:37,038 --> 00:05:41,944
My call to action rendered as a teal box inside another teal box,

96
00:05:41,944 --> 00:05:44,737
twice the height it should have been.

97
00:05:44,737 --> 00:05:46,548
And the CSS was correct.

98
00:05:47,348 --> 00:05:49,045
Two elements matched.

99
00:05:49,045 --> 00:05:53,005
Wagtail seven already wraps every block in a div,

100
00:05:53,005 --> 00:05:57,773
and that div already carries a class named after the block.

101
00:05:57,773 --> 00:05:59,147
Block dash c t a.

102
00:05:59,147 --> 00:06:05,774
My template added a class with exactly the same name, so the styling landed twice.

103
00:06:06,574 --> 00:06:11,661
So delete the wrapper class from your templates and style Wagtail's instead.

104
00:06:11,661 --> 00:06:16,881
It is fewer lines, and every block you add later gets a wrapper class for free

105
00:06:16,881 --> 00:06:18,688
without you doing anything.

106
00:06:19,488 --> 00:06:22,231
And this is the payoff, in the admin.

107
00:06:22,231 --> 00:06:26,086
One plus button opens a menu of exactly five things,

108
00:06:26,086 --> 00:06:29,126
with the icons and labels we set in Meta.

109
00:06:29,126 --> 00:06:32,388
Add them, drag them into any order you like.

110
00:06:32,388 --> 00:06:37,652
The editor gets freedom, you keep control of what the page can contain.

111
00:06:37,652 --> 00:06:40,914
That is the whole reason StreamField exists.

112
00:06:41,714 --> 00:06:44,781
Two settings, same word, different jobs.

113
00:06:44,781 --> 00:06:51,146
Block counts on the stream block limits how many of a block type the whole page may

114
00:06:51,146 --> 00:06:51,529
have.

115
00:06:51,529 --> 00:06:56,667
Max num on the list block limits how many items go inside one list.

116
00:06:56,667 --> 00:06:58,967
One services section per page.

117
00:06:58,967 --> 00:07:00,884
Up to six services in it.

118
00:07:01,684 --> 00:07:03,682
And here is the home page.

119
00:07:03,682 --> 00:07:06,986
A paragraph, a services grid, a pull quote,

120
00:07:06,986 --> 00:07:12,212
and a call to action whose button link came out of the page chooser.

121
00:07:12,212 --> 00:07:16,438
Four blocks, four templates, all ordered by the editor.

122
00:07:17,238 --> 00:07:18,725
And the About page.

123
00:07:18,725 --> 00:07:23,266
That first paragraph is the one we wrote in episode three,

124
00:07:23,266 --> 00:07:29,293
carried across by the data migration, with a new heading block underneath it.

125
00:07:29,293 --> 00:07:30,624
Nothing was lost.

126
00:07:31,424 --> 00:07:33,938
Commit, and tag.

127
00:07:34,738 --> 00:07:37,622
Next episode, images and documents.

128
00:07:37,622 --> 00:07:42,071
Renditions, focal points, and the image chooser block,

129
00:07:42,071 --> 00:07:45,532
which is the block everybody wanted today.

130
00:07:46,332 --> 00:07:52,187
Next episode, images and documents.

131
00:07:52,187 --> 00:07:55,532
Thanks for watching.
